 [17592186175937 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186275209 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175937 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186275210 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175937 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186535993 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175937 #edb/ref 1039 "Computing Covariance in Context" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175937 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186175747 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175937 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "cee807c1-dd86-5b0e-a595-5c5754c47e4c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176135 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186176655 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176135 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186176656 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176135 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186176657 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176135 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186176658 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176135 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176135 #edb/ref 1045 "Covariance" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176135 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186176655 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176135 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049126 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176135 #edb/ref 1050 600.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176135 #edb/ref 1050 600.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186176135 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "275b0afa-011e-599e-83db-08f12becae8b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176655 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186176656 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176655 #edb/ref 1061 217080 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176655 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a9620c91-7f1f-5c90-81f9-15b63580b9b6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176655 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186176950 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176656 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186176657 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176656 #edb/ref 1061 217081 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176656 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7c94f745-4162-5e7d-841a-0a7d3f00e84a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176656 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186175936 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176657 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186176658 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176657 #edb/ref 1061 217084 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176657 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "48e20fe8-234e-5200-b8a8-908f518d0da4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176657 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186175937 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176658 #edb/ref 1061 217087 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176658 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2661268b-e076-5805-af10-02ffd1c3fc5e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176658 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186176951 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176950 #edb/ref 1064 "Given two finite data sets of equal length, say,\n\n$$\nx=\\big\\{ x_1,x_2, \\ldots, x_n \\big\\}, \\qquad \ny=\\big\\{ y_1,y_2, \\ldots, y_n \\big\\},\n$$\n\nthe **covariance** between $x$ and $y,$ denoted by $\\textrm{Cov}(x,y),$ is a measure that evaluates the extent to which $x$ and $y$ change together.\n\n- A positive covariance means that if $x$ increases, then $y$ is also likely to increase:\n\n![](images/bb/bbfae3f0fb38bc8652cd26716e4b0b128cf1f2039350267034d97161d7f5dac4.png)\n\n- A negative covariance means that if $x$ increases, then $y$ is likely to decrease:\n\n![](images/fd/fd45053fdc39f070e3438c3b8c61fe01613201595cfe00bd4cc6c6e481bf73ab.png)\n\n- A covariance of zero (or close to zero) indicates that there is no *linear* relationship between $x$ and $y.$\n\n![](images/a5/a58fa4d40d77af23df86b5bd8eaca3119b93bc9ea97cc435eb4e53ba2777b071.png)\n\n \n\n**Watch Out!** A covariance of zero does *not* mean that $x$ and $y$ are not related. It simply means the relationship between them is not linear. To illustrate, consider the image below.\n\n![](images/a4/a4bdbf92e691174644dda9b9a84acb1b896c0436afb221501dc10b4635841539.png)\n\n \n\nThe (nonlinear) relationship shown above is $y=x^2.$ However, it can be shown that $\\textrm{Cov}(x,y) = 0$ for this data set.\n\nTo calculate $\\textrm{Cov}(x,y),$ we use the following formula: \n\n$$\n\\textrm{Cov}(x,y) =  \\dfrac{1}{n} \\sum\\limits_{i=1}^n (x_i - \\overline{x})(y_i - \\overline{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overline{x}$  and $\\overline{y}$ denote the means of $x$ and $y$ respectively.\n\n**Note**: This formula for the covariance assumes that $x$ and $y$ are drawn from a *population*. There is a slightly different formula for covariance when $x$ and $y$ are sample data. However, we won't worry about the difference for now." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176950 #edb/ref 1065 10301 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176950 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "da03b3e7-b452-59b9-b81e-5dd75cea02a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176950 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176951 #edb/ref 1064 "Variance measures the spread of a *single* data set $x$ around its mean value $\\overline{x}.$ On the other hand, covariance measures the relationship between *two* data sets $x$ and $y.$\n\nThe (population) covariance of the data sets\n\n$$\nx=\\big\\{ x_1,x_2, \\ldots, x_n \\big\\}, \\qquad  \ny=\\big\\{ y_1,y_2, \\ldots, y_n \\big\\}\n$$\n\n \n\nis given by \n\n$$\n\\textrm{Cov}(x,y) =  \\dfrac{1}{n} \\sum\\limits_{i=1}^n (x_i - \\overline{x})(y_i - \\overline{y}).\n$$\n\nIf we compare a single data set, say $x$, against itself using our formula for covariance, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,x) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & ={\\sigma }^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\sigma^2$ denotes the variance of $x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176951 #edb/ref 1065 10305 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176951 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "42b9ca98-be0b-50e0-9b90-f3e38732fcd0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176951 #edb/ref 1067 "The Connection Between Variance and Covariance" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266439 #edb/ref 1080 "19" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266439 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266439 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "20dc8ecd-d3e7-5b4f-99fd-e340125220ff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266669 #edb/ref 1080 "12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266669 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266669 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3bf4b541-acde-57aa-9576-c308680b6c1c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267179 #edb/ref 1080 "15" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267179 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267179 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "756ab281-4dfc-522d-827d-e6219862d3f3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267242 #edb/ref 1080 "16" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267242 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267242 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7bdc279d-d8bf-5db2-99d2-0230056971c0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267359 #edb/ref 1080 "10" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267359 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267359 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "88b47b3a-e1eb-56e3-8e5d-f4a75117a124" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267466 #edb/ref 1080 "7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267466 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267466 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "939eb21e-65d9-50c2-9f13-2a9c5beb9a7e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267495 #edb/ref 1080 "10" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267495 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267495 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9717bf9a-a903-59dd-8538-a467393f5b22" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268011 #edb/ref 1080 "6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268011 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268011 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d0ce4537-3c51-5a6d-afe7-2fec5be72a5e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268228 #edb/ref 1080 "6.5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268228 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268228 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e9e26f0a-1b74-5e94-b5a5-bc4046928faa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268386 #edb/ref 1080 "4.5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268386 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268386 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fec05032-593e-5492-9092-712f5a38fa46" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268430 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186267359 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268430 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186267466 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268430 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186268011 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268430 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186268228 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268430 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186268386 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268430 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268430 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268430 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186267466 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268430 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "0c10a926-37e1-5762-a3bc-8007b371df78" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268542 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186266439 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268542 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186266669 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268542 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186267179 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268542 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186267242 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268542 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186267495 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268542 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268542 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268542 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186267242 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268542 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "4eb084b7-92a4-50b3-ab5e-874dc5122653" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268978 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186268542 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268978 #edb/ref 1069 "q-134168" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268978 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268978 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\text{Cov}(x,y)$ for the following data sets:\n\n$$\nx=\\{-4,\\,2,\\,6,\\,8\\},\\,y=\\{2,\\,-9,\\,3,\\,12\\}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268978 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e3d02030-a1e3-5cc4-b308-6cf0c2ca9175" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268978 #edb/ref 1074 "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x=\\{{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}\\}$ and $y=\\{{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the means:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot ((-4)+2+6+8) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =3 \\\\ \\overset{―}{y} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (2+(-9)+3+12) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-4-3)(2-2)+(2-3)(-9-2)+(6-3)(3-2)+(8-3)(12-2)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-7)(0)+(-1)(-11)+(3)(1)+(5)(10)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[0+11+3+50] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 64 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268981 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186268430 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268981 #edb/ref 1069 "q-134173" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268981 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268981 #edb/ref 1071 "| **Time Spent Practicing, \nin hours ($x$)** | $4$ | $5$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Points Scored ($y$)** | $4$ | $8$ | $12$ | $16$ |\n\nThe table above shows Mary's time practicing her jump shot each week and the number of points she scores in the Friday varsity basketball game. Compute the covariance of the data sets given that the means are $\\overset{―}{x}=6$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=10.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268981 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0a871439-561a-57b5-a2c7-bd992bf74497" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268981 #edb/ref 1074 "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x=\\{{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}\\}$ and $y=\\{{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(4-6)(4-10)+(5-6)(8-10)+(7-6)(12-10)+(8-6)(16-10)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-2)(-6)+(-1)(-2)+(1)(2)+(2)(6)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[12+2+2+12] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 28 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565672 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186566296 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565672 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186566299 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565672 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186566300 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565672 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565672 #edb/ref 1045 "Covariance" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565672 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186566300 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565672 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565672 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049126 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565672 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "b71da19e-d859-5f56-b0d6-c095ea38a156" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565876 #edb/ref 1080 "10" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565876 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565876 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7c9e72d7-60a7-512f-af6c-41536483d13a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175921