\\,4,\\,-4,\\,4\\},\\,y=\\{-1,\\,-2,\\,7,\\,4\\}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566235 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "64eb2650-1408-5539-acdf-62ad07765696" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566235 #edb/ref 1074 "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x=\\{{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}\\}$ and $y=\\{{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the means:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (4+4+(-4)+4) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =2 \\\\ \\overset{―}{y} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot ((-1)+(-2)+7+4) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(4-2)(-1-2)+(4-2)(-2-2)+(-4-2)(7-2)+(4-2)(4-2)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(2)(-3)+(2)(-4)+(-6)(5)+(2)(2)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[-6-8-30+4] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (-40) \\\\  & =-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566296 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6dca6571-a5ec-5352-8411-48e22666e7db" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566296 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186268981 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566299 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186566296 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566299 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9360c9ad-0d01-58c3-bea9-ccb29100787e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566299 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186268978 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566300 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186566299 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566300 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "96cf8720-bbba-5c5c-9ffc-98b6e94d3c0b" #edb/ref 